\par\par \b \uc2  RESEARCH ALERT-Wider Hungary forint band unlikely. \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 November 1998\par 17:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Nov 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  will leave the forint's 4.5-percent-wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band unchanged in the short-term, brokerage Bankar said on Tuesday, taking issue with a country update by investment bank Warburg Dillon Read. \par \par \uc2  Warburg said earlier on Tuesday that it expected the National Bank of Hungary (NBH) to widen the flotation band to 10 or 15 percent in an unforced move at the beginning of 1999. \par \par \uc2  Such a measure would give the NBH more flexibility in its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reduce the vulnerability of the forint to speculative attacks, London-based Warburg analysts said in the report. \par \par \uc2  Laszlo Makay, analyst at Hungarian brokerage Bankar, said a widening of the band would not be reasonable in the near term and could be much smaller than 10-15 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is currently strengthening within the band due to the renewed confidence in Hungary by foreign investors, so there is no need for any change," he said. \par \par \uc2  The forint ended at a new 10-week high at 0.2 percent below parity on Tuesday, boosted by a slow but steady capital inflow after heavy withdrawals in the wake of Russia's financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  Makay said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had suggested in its monetary policy guidelines that the forint band might be widened only if inflation drops below 10 percent and stays there. \par \par \uc2  Inflation ran at 12.5 percent in September. \par \par \uc2  Makay said a near-term widening of the band was also unlikely because it could shake confidence in the exchange rate regime and increase risk premiums. He said the NBH was interested in a stable capital inflow. \par \par \uc2  ((Sandor Peto, Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4044 budapest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926dub305f2t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
