\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Hungary \highlight\uc2  will not widen  \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention \highlight\uc2  band. \b0\par\par\uc2 225 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 1998\par 14:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Sept 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no plans to widen its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, which now allows the forint to float in a 4.5 percent range against a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Gyorgy Suranyi said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "I rule out the possibility of widening of the band because for the time being it might create depreciation in a wider band and any depreciation is not reasonable for the time being," Suranyi told Reuters Television in a telephone interview. \par \par \uc2  There has been widespread speculation in recent weeks that the bank might widen the band, which allows the forint to float against a basket of marks and dollars, in response to foreign investors cashing in their Hungarian shares and withdrawing from the Hungarian market. \par \par \uc2  Suranyi said depreciating the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was "really not required by any economic indicator and it would create a pressure on inflation as well". \par \par \uc2  "If there is a need for adjustment it is rather the interest rate and - if it is a longer term development, I mean if the outlook has to be revised on the medium and long term - then there is a need rather for a fiscal than an exchange rate adjustment," Suranyi said. \par \par \uc2  ((Michael Roddy, Budapest newsroom ++ 36 1 327 4040 \par \par \uc2  budapest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du9f015cb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich