\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary O/N rates down, forint seen up vs basket. \b0\par\par\uc2 215 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1998\par 09:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  0650 GMT - Hungarian overnight rates traded at 16.50/625 percent in abundant liquidity while the forint, which closed at the weaker end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band on Wednesday, was seen firming on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  * Overnight rates were down from the open of 16.875 percent and Wednesday's close of 16.75/875 percent with one or two significant borrowers on the market, traders said. \par \par \uc2  * The forint was seen strengthening during the day to about 2.0 percent below parity from its close near the bottom of the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 4.5-percent-wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, at about 2.20 percent below parity, traders said. \par \par \uc2  * Against the dollar, the forint was quoted at 0650 GMT at 220.55/70. \par \par \uc2  * Traders said they expected the forint to firm because of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling, but they were not sure whether higher levels would hold. \par \par \uc2  * Traders did not expect \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the forint. At 2.25 percent below parity, which is the weakest point in the band, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  * The forint trades against a basket composed of 30 percent dollar and 70 percent mark. \par \par \uc2  (Full reports to follow.). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du9a00tj2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\