\par\par \b \uc2  Hungarian Forint Weakens Early But  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Idle \b0\par\par\uc2 304 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1998\par 11:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is at its weakest spot on its trading band early Thursday, but traders said no \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected since the weakening has occurred in very thin liquidity. \par \par \uc2  Around 0850 GMT the forint was at 2.25% on the weak side of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band, from about 2.20% at Wednesday's close. A higher percentage on the weak side of the band indicates a lower forint. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allows the forint to move a maximum 2.25% from the midpoint, which is fixed using a basket of 30% dollar and 70% Deutsche mark. The bank devalues the forint by 0.8% each month against the basket. \par \par \uc2  "Demand (for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against forints) is minimal so there's no pressure for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said dealer Zoltan Kalman at Hypo Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  The forint has weakened partly on expiring \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures and partly on speculation, Kalman added. \par \par \uc2  The presence of some foreign banks in the market means the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't been seen doing any deals, Kalman said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0855 GMT, the dollar was at HUF220.17-220.37, down from HUF223.20-223.40 late Wednesday. The mark was at HUF129.18-129.28, up from HUF128.31-128.41. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the forint Wednesday at HUF222.27 to the dollar, up from HUF221.97 Tuesday. It fixed the forint at HUF128.50 to the mark Wednesday, up from HUF128.27 Tuesday. Thursday's fixings will be released after 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Three-month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 16.60%\par Thursday, unchanged from Wednesday.\par    -By Margit Feher; 36-1-267-0623; mfeher@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 10-09-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0926GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du9a07sc6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
