\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary forint seen slighty up in Sept-Citibank. \b0\par\par\uc2 250 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 1998\par 14:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Sept 3 (Reuters) - Hungary's forint is expected to firm slightly this month after recent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  meant to boost confidence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Hungarian brokerage Citibank Securities said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "We expect HUF to remain in the range of 1.2 and 1.7 percent below parity, i.e. in the weaker half of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band in September," Citibank said in an update on Hungarian markets. \par \par \uc2  The forint has been trading at record low levels since early last week, near the weak end of the 4.5 percent wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, pounded by the withdrawal of capital by foreign investors covering losses they suffered in Russia. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent up to $100 million on market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  according to dealers' estimates, so as to support the forint. \par \par \uc2  The forint stood at two percent below parity at noon, down from Wednesday's close of 1.85 percent below midline. \par \par \uc2  Citibank said the forint would return to the positive territory of the band, where it traded for most of the past three years, only if foreign investors' confidence recovers and $1 billion flows into Hungary's markets from abroad. \par \par \uc2  The brokerage also said Hungary's consumer inflation was expected to remain close to July's 14.1 percent level in August. The statistical office will publish the August figure on September 11. \par \par \uc2  ((Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4044 budapest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2