\par\par \b \uc2  WRAP: Emerging Mkts Shares,  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Tumble On Russia \b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 August 1998\par 13:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LONDON (Dow Jones)--With no end to Russia's economic crisis in sight, Eastern European and African stock markets look set to continue to fall after sustaining more heavy losses Friday. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are also falling, with central banks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit the damage. \par \par \uc2  As shares on the Budapest Stock Exchange fell 12% at the opening following declines of 14% Thursday, the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stabilize the forint (HUF). \par \par \uc2  "It's complete panic selling," said John Barnett, equities analyst at Raiffeisen Securities & Investment in Budapest. Asked how far the market could drop, he said, "It's impossible to say at this point." \par \par \uc2  The Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on three occasions to support the lira (TRL) as shares fell 5.5% following Thursday's 13% decline. The country's financial markets weren't comforted by assurances from Prime Minister Mesut Yilmaz that the government will stick to monetary policy targets agreed to with the International Monetary Fund, and won't go on a spending spree ahead of elections in April. \par \par \uc2  Russia's share market was relatively stable, down just 1.25%, or 0.79 of a point, to 62.41 points following a string of heavy declines in recent sessions. \par \par \uc2  However, concerns over the future of the country's economy mounted as details of Prime Minister-Designate Victor Chernomyrdin's economic policy began to emerge. As part of a plan to be presented to parliament Monday, the prime minister is likely to propose printing rubles to meet wage arrears and shore up the country's banks, as well as re-nationalization of strategic industries. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 28-08-98 \par \par \uc2  1130GMT \par \par \uc2  1192 4207 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8s07cpk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
