\par\par \b \uc2  CSFB sees Hungary interest rate cut delayed. \b0\par\par\uc2 162 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 1998\par 09:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Aug 27 (Reuters) - The Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may hold back regular rate cuts due the effect of the Russian crisis on the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Credit Suisse First Boston (CSFB) said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "Although Hungary has relatively minor trade links with Russia (which took 5.1 percent of its exports in 1997), the forint has come under pressure recently," CSFB said in its weekly update on emerging Europe. \par \par \uc2  On Monday the forint fell to a historical low of 2.05 percent below parity in the 4.5-percent-wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band before recovering. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBH) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least twice to cut forint fluctuations (within the band) that it said were unjustified by domestic economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stance also suggests that any further interest rate cuts will be delayed," CSFB added. \par \par \uc2  ((Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4047 budapest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8r01qfd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
