\par\par \b \uc2  Hungarian Forint Ends Sharply Dn, Ctrl Bk Doesn't  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 1998\par 15:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint weakened steadily Thursday afternoon to record lows against the dollar, but the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't repeat Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the forint, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At the close of regular trading in Budapest at around 1300 GMT, the forint was at a record low of about 2.00% from the midpoint on the weak side of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band, softer from 1.3% at midmorning and also weaker from 1.25% at Wednesday's close. \par \par \uc2  On the soft side of the band, a higher percentage means the forint is weaker. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allows the forint to move a maximum 2.25% from the midpoint, which is fixed using a basket of 30% dollar and 70% Deutsche mark. The bank devalues the forint by 0.8% each month against the basket. \par \par \uc2  Hurt by a 14% decline in Hungarian stocks Thursday, the forint reached a record low against the dollar. Around 1300 GMT, the dollar was at HUF228.30-228.50, up sharply from HUF226.60-226.90 at midmorning and also up from HUF226.30-226.70 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The mark was at HUF126.27-126.32, up from HUF125.53-125.58 at midmorning and also higher from HUF126.10-126.15 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "If nothing new comes out and if we don't hear any news from the government or the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we're going to reach the top of the trading band," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at K&H Bank in Budapest, referring to the forint's weakest point of 2.25% from the midpoint. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 27-08-98 \par \par \uc2  1321GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8r07aqx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
