\par\par \b \uc2  INSTANT VIEW -  \highlight22\uc2 Hungary \highlight\uc2  c.bank forint  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 1998\par 16:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Aug 26 (Reuters) - The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBH) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly on Wednesday to protect the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from what it said were swings "unjustified by macroeconomic indicators. \par \par \uc2  Following are analysts' comments. \par \par \uc2  PETER BIHARI, BUDAPEST BANK, BUDAPEST \par \par \uc2  "I think it has less of a financial explanation, and it was more to calm investors' minds and to demonstrate the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's commitment (towards the forint)." \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor stated repeatedly during the last few days that if the need arises, the NBH would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect the forint. The move was probably (intended to) demonstrate that these were not just words." \par \par \uc2  NIGEL RENDELL, SANTANDER INVESTMENT BANK, LONDON \par \par \uc2  "I think it's a direct result of what's going on in Russia and other emerging markets. All emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  seemed to be under pressure and several central banks have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  "I think \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  largely just to try to keep things on an even keel. I don't think there is anything more sort of sinister than that." \par \par \uc2  PETER DURONELLY, BUDAPEST FUND MANAGEMENT \par \par \uc2  "I have heard that it was only a small amount. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wanted to reassure the market that it is there and is ready to protect the forint. \par \par \uc2  "There is no attack against the forint, it is only that foreigners reallocating their portfolio withdraw funds, partly due to the Russian events. \par \par \uc2  "The NBH could reassure the market more easily if it declared it would not widen the (4.5 percent wide) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band until December. Fears that the band would be widened hinder speculation (in favour of the forint) return to the market." ((Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4047 budapest.newsoom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  ((Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4047 budapest.newsoom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8q01ku4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
