\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS- \highlight22\uc2 Hungary \highlight\uc2  c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to calm markets. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sandor Peto \par \uc2 669 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 1998\par 18:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Aug 26 (Reuters) - The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBH) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly on the interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday, in a step which analysts said was aimed at reassuring investors hit by emerging market jitters. \par \par \uc2  "I think it has less of a financial explanation and it was more to calm investors' minds and to demonstrate the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's commitment (towards the forint)," said Budapest Bank analyst Peter Bihari. \par \par \uc2  The NBH said it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut forint fluctuations that it said were unjustified by domestic economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  "The main reason for the current \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was to soothe the exaggerated exchange rate movements unjustified by macroeconomic indicators," NBH Managing Director Adam Farkas told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "On the other hand, we wanted to lend confidence to the market," he said, adding the forint was still within its 4.5 percent wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band when the NBH entered the market. \par \par \uc2  It was the second time that the NBH had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's crawling peg devaluation regime was launched in March 1995, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The NBH declined to disclose how much foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  it spent on supporting the forint, but market participants said it was a small amount. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came when the forint traded at 1.5 to 1.6 percent below parity, weaker than its all-time low of 2.05 percent below midrange reached earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  The forint has been jittery since May due to the spillover impact of Asian and Russian market turbulence. It has been repeatedly breaking through earlier record lows since last week as foreign investors covered losses suffered in Russia. \par \par \uc2  The forint finished at 1.4 percent below parity after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and at 226.30/80 against the dollar, down from Tuesday's close of 225.20/40. \par \par \uc2  An analyst said the NBH took pre-emptive action within the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band because it feared the forint could fall to the bottom of the range. \par \par \uc2  "We believe the main reason for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  inside the band was that it expected the forint exchange rate to further fall during the day, eventually reaching the (weak) frontier of the band," said Takarek Broker's Tamas David. \par \par \uc2  Market participants said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came after Hungarian shares and government bonds extended recent losses mainly caused by foreign investors' sales. \par \par \uc2  The Budapest Stock Exchange's BUX index closed at 6,386.36 points, down by 384.10 points or 5.67 percent, 29.22 percent below its all-time high of 9,022.95 points reaced on April 23. \par \par \uc2  Hungarian government bond yields rose. \par \par \uc2  "The yield on one-year paper was 16.4 percent yesterday, but they were sold even at 16.85 percent today, while two-year bonds went up to 15.35/40 from 16.2 percent," said CA IB Securities trader Tamas Puskas. \par \par \uc2  Market participants agreed with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that Hungary's economic fundamentals were strong, but said the country's markets could not avoid the contagion started by Russia, at least in the short run. \par \par \uc2  "We can expect a bad and changeable market, depending on what happens in Russia," Puskas said. He said funds withdrawn from Hungarian government securities were much below the capital which flowed out from Polish bonds. \par \par \uc2  The NBH did not rule out the possibility that it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if Wednesday's move does not calm the market. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts said the forint's weakening showed that capital was flowing out from the country through an illiquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, rather than indicating that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was attacked by speculators. \par \par \uc2  "The NBH could reassure the market more easily if it declared it would not widen the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band until December," said Budapest Fund Management Peter Duronelly. \par \par \uc2  "Fears that the band would be widened hinder speculation (in favour of the forint) return to the market," he added. \par \par \uc2  ((Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4044 budapest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8q01kk7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
