\par\par \b \uc2  CORRECTED - Hungary policy makers to discuss bad Russia impact. \b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 August 1998\par 19:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  In Budapest story "Hungary policy makers to discuss bad Russia impact", please read in sixth paragraph, "...still remained below its previous record low at one percent below midrange." instead of "...still remained below its previous record high at one percent below midrange." (corrects to clarify that it was a previous negative record.) \par \par \uc2  A corrected story follows. \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Aug 24 (Reuters) - Hungarian Prime Minister Viktor Orban said on Monday he would meet economic policy makers on Tuesday to discuss how the negative impacts of Russia's financial woes on Hungarian markets could be tackled. \par \par \uc2  Orban was quoted by the national news agency MTI as saying he would meet \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Gyorgy Suranyi, Finance Minister Zsigmond Jarai, Economic Minister Attila Chikan and state privatisation agency APV head Gyula Gansperger. \par \par \uc2  The Budapest Stock Exchange's BUX index fell 6.61 percent to 7.189.28 on Monday mainly due to selling by foreigners concerned over Russia's political and financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  The BUX eased about 25 percent since its April 23 record high of 9,022.95 points, mainly due to concerns over emerging markets triggered by Russia's and Asian economic problems. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBH) warned Monday that it was ready for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect the forint, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell Monday morning to a record low of 2.05 percent below midrange in the 4.5 percent wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  range. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose to a close of 1.00/30 percent below parity after the NBH's announcement, but still remained below its previous record low at one percent below midrange. \par \par \uc2  Orban spoke to journalists after returning from Poland, where he met Prime Minister Jerzy Buzek. \par \par \uc2  Selling by investors covering losses in Russia have been weighing on Polish and Czech markets also, but the zloty and the Czech crown rebounded in thin volume on Monday after Russian President Boris Yeltsin replaced its cabinet on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  Hungarian politicians and market participants have said investors fears over Russia's problems affected Hungary's markets despite that economic fundamentals were strong and did not justify falls in share prices and the forint exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  ((Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4044 budapest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8o01e3d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
