\par\par \b \uc2  Hungarian Forint Plunges -3: Investors Ignore Fundamentals \b0\par\par\uc2 309 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 1998\par 15:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  By the close at 1300 GMT, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to have stabilized, hovering within a few basis points around the midpoint on the band. At one point the forint slipped to about 0.2% on the weak side of the band. \par \par \uc2  At the time of the forint's last steep fall, just after Hungary's parliamentary elections in May, the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it wouldn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market other as long as the forint remains with the 4.5% trading band. \par \par \uc2  "Today is a terrible day market-wise," said Istvan Racz, director at Credit Suisse First Boston in Budapest, pointing to the 7.8% drop the Budapest Stock Exchange's BUX index suffered Tuesday. "Basically, it's about Russia. I think we are severely affected by this." \par \par \uc2  Racz also said that the market may also be unclear about the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's intentions regarding monetary policy, following the announcement Monday of a relatively steep cut in interest rates. \par \par \uc2  As reported, the bank said that effective Aug. 15 it will cut its overnight reverse repo rate to 13.5% from 14.5%, while cutting the overnight active repo rate to 20.5% from 22.5%, also effective Aug. 15. \par \par \uc2  The repo rates are the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tools for adding and draining liquidity from the interbank money market. \par \par \uc2  As investors run for the exits, they appear to be ignoring fundamentals, evidenced by the market's disregard for a string of positive data Tuesday on Hungary's inflation, trade balance and budget deficit, Racz said. \par \par \uc2  "Unfortunately, there is a lack of appreciation of the fact that Hungary's external viability is still at a pretty high level," Racz said. \par \par \uc2  -By Jack Grone; 36-1-267-0622; jgrone@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 11-08-98 \par \par \uc2  1305GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8b06rcb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
