\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary forint weakens vs basket on energy payment. \b0\par\par\uc2 231 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 1998\par 13:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, June 26 (Reuters) - The Hungarian forint closed weaker against the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar/mark \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket on Friday as the payment of energy bills triggered demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The forint finished at 0.6 percent above parity within the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (NBH) 4.5-percent-wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, down from Thursday's close at 1.1 percent, they said. \par \par \uc2  "It was the time to pay oil bills," said Jozsef Laczi, dealer at ING Bank. "This weighed a lot (on the forint) and the impact was enhanced by speculation." \par \par \uc2  "It's the end of the month," said Peter Piros of Europai Kereskedelmi Bank. "(The forint) is weaker probably due to the end-month (import) bills." \par \par \uc2  Traders said the payment of energy bills takes place regularly at the end of a month, resulting in the outflow of significant amount of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Piros added that the forint was likely to remain around current levels early next week. \par \par \uc2  The NBH fixed the forint at 217.85 to the dollar, compared to 217.04 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The forint floats within the NBH's 4.5-percent-wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  range against a basket made up 30 percent dollar and 70 percent mark. \par \par \uc2  ((Emese Bartha, Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4047 budapest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6q020wc\par }\page {\par\fs2