\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary forint opens firmer against basket, dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, June 4 (Reuters) - The Hungarian forint opened firmer against both the dollar and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket as market nerves calmed a bit following an opposition victory in elections on May 24, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The forint was quoted at 0750 GMT at 1.6 percent above parity, up from Wednesday's close of 1.15 above parity and Thursday's opening at 1.00/10 percent. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the forint was quoted at 212.50/70, up from Wednesday's close of 213.20/30 and Thursday's opening of 212.50/213.00. \par \par \uc2  "Maybe the uncertainty following the elections has ended," said Peter Szurjes, trader at Kereskedelmi es Hitelbank. "The stock exchange also did well (on Wednesday). People are trying to close their basket positions," he said. \par \par \uc2  The forint fell to record lows just above the middle of the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (NBH) 4.5-percent-wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  range last week due to uncertainty over the composition and policies of a new government and investor worries over emerging markets, especially Russia. \par \par \uc2  Centre-right Fidesz Hungarian Civic Party won the elections on May 24 over the ruling Socialists and is expected to set up a three-party coalition government over the next few weeks. \par \par \uc2  Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  buyers were encouraged on Wednesday by a 7.5 percent rise in the Budapest bourse's BUX index. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the forint could continue to firm this week but a low turnover on Wednesday had showed that market participants were still cautious. The Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected to remain volatile until the new government is formed. \par \par \uc2  Szurjes said that the forint should continue to strengthen on Thursday and could end at around 1.8/9 percent above parity in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  range. \par \par \uc2  The forint trades against a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket made of 30 percent dollar and 70 percent German mark. \par \par \uc2  ((Daniel Langenkamp, Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4043 budapest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6403p7q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
