\par\par \b \uc2  Hungarian Forint Steady At Midmorning After Early Weakening \b0\par\par\uc2 231 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 1998\par 10:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint (HUF) is stable at midmorning Friday after weakening within its trading band earlier in the session. \par \par \uc2  Traders expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to settle into a narrow range following Thursday's wild fluctuations. \par \par \uc2  Around 0830 GMT in highly illiquid trade, the forint was around 0.70% on the strong side of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band, down from 0.98% in late trading Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Selling by foreigners worried about the policies of Hungary's incoming conservative government sparked a steep slide in the forint early Thursday to its lowest levels since the present exchange-rate mechanism was instituted in 1995. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  later recovered, with the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  denying market rumors that it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the forint either directly or by prodding a major commercial bank to place a big buy order for forints. \par \par \uc2  "There's still some buying interest for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Friday), but it's slowed down a bit (from the start of the session)," said Peter Luczo, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Inter-Europa Bank in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  Around 0830 GMT, the dollar was at HUF214.33-214.85, up from HUF213.59-214.49 in late trading Thursday. The mark was at HUF119.90-120.40, up slightly from HUF119.76-120.76. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 29-05-98 \par \par \uc2  0851GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 1