\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary forint opens firmer vs  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  basket. \b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 1998\par 10:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, May 29 (Reuters) - Hungary's forint opened firmer against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket on Friday as it continued its recovery after Thursday's panic selling, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Hungarian unit opened at 1.2 percent above parity within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 4.5 percent wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  range, compared to Thursday's close of one percent. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the forint traded in wide ranges and stood at 214.25/50 in early deals, slightly down from Thursday's close of 213.82/214.20. \par \par \uc2  At one point on Thursday, the forint dropped to 0.3 percent above parity on speculation in a very illiquid market until a large deal in the afternoon brought its level back up. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling dollars to support the Hungarian unit but the NBH denied this. \par \par \uc2  Joszef Laczi, dealer at ING Bank, said that if there is not a strong reaction on Friday from foreign investors to Thursday's falls the forint will contiue to move back towards the resistance level (bid). \par \par \uc2  "I believe the foreigners were very surprised and there is evidence thay may buy (\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) today," he said. "That would stop the forint moving back to the bid and could even reverse the trend." \par \par \uc2  The market has been concerned this week by financial problems in Russia and about possible changes in economic policy in Hungary, where a centre-right coalition is expected to take over from the outgoing Socialist-led coalition. \par \