\par\par \b \uc2  Hungarian Ctrl Bk/Denies -2: No Opinion On Forint's Swings \b0\par\par\uc2 212 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 1998\par 14:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (Dow Jones)--The National Bank of Hungary denied rumors in \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Hungarian forint. \par \par \uc2  A spokesman from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made the comment to Dow Jones Newswires after a wild day on the forint market, during which the forint weakened to unprecedented lows in the morning, then strengthened sharply against the dollar and the Deutsche mark early in the afternoon. \par \par \uc2  The spokesman said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no opinion on the forint's moves Thursday, and added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  believes the forint's current trading band is wide enough to accommodate the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's swings. \par \par \uc2  Some \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers in Budapest said an early-afternoon order to buy forints, worth an estimated $10 million to $20 million, may have driven the forint higher in Thursday's illiquid market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allows the forint to move a maximum 2.25% from the midpoint of the band, which is fixed using a basket of 30% dollar and 70% Deutsche mark. The bank devalues the forint by 0.9% each month against the basket. \par \par \uc2  -By Jack Grone and Margit Feher; 361-267-0622 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 28-05-98 \par \par \uc2  1239GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5s04kt5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\p