\par\par \b \uc2  Edgy post-poll Hungary markets eye foreigners. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sandor Peto \par \uc2 734 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 1998\par 19:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, May 25 (Reuters) - Hungary's edgy markets are waiting to see how foreigners will react on Tuesday to the Socialist government's toppling by a rightist party in weekend elections. \par \par \uc2  The forint weakened on Monday and the Budapest Stock Exchange BUX index fell 8.7 percent on sales by local investors after the centre-right Fidesz Hungarian Civic Party beat the ruling ex-communist Socialist Party in Sunday's polls, but public holidays in Britain and the United States limited foreign interest. \par \par \uc2  "Tomorrow will be critical," said CAIB Securities analyst Csaba Ludanyi. "Foreigners are not so discouraged that they would get rid of their securities at any price...but we will see what happens to the forint." \par \par \uc2  The forint closed at 1.55 to 1.60 percent above parity in the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBH)'s 4.5-percent-wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  range, compared to Friday's close of 1.95 percent above midrange. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has usually traded at 2.25 percent above parity for the past two years, weakened in modest trade as domestic dealers speculated on uncertainty over the composition of the new government. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  later this week if the forint continued to weaken on jitters over the new government's economic policy, increased by expectations that Fidesz will form a coalition with the agrarian-based Smallholders. \par \par \uc2  They said \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic fundamentals remained strong and a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could successfully prevent excessive securities sales triggered by political uncertainty. \par \par \uc2  "There may be a panic-triggered selling wave, and in this case it would make sense to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Csaba Ludanyi of CAIB Securities. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said a key issue was how foreign investors would react to the post-election nervousness. \par \par \uc2  "Uncertainty may last for a while and it's a question of how long the patience of foreigners endures and how long they bear losses," said Zoltan Bakonyi of K&H Securities. "I think that they are still patient." \par \par \uc2  But some analysts said the forint might suffer a substantial further weakening if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and this might discourage many foreign investors even though the forint was expected to remain well within the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. \par \par \uc2  BNP-Dresdner Securities analyst Zoltan Kurali said the forint might fall to the middle of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  range. \par \par \uc2  In that case the National Bank (NBH) might return to fixing the yield on its one-year bonds instead of letting it float freely, so as to support a yield curve which would ensure acceptable yields to investors. \par \par \uc2  Other analysts said the NBH might prevent an excessive weakening of the forint by buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Ludanyi said some investors who had sold \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures in proportion to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's basket - 30 percent dollar and 70 percent mark - might begin to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent further losses if the forint fell excessively. \par \par \uc2  Domestic investors who had bought stocks on credits might continue to sell their shares, he added. \par \par \uc2  Most analysts said the forint could face substantial pressure until the new government clarified its intentions on economic policy, but sound fundamentals would prevent a crisis. \par \par \uc2  "Macroeconomic figures are still positive," Kurali said. \par \par \uc2  Some investors recalled that the Polish economy had performed well after the centre-right ousted a government led by the ex-communist party late last year, another analyst added. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the stock exchange was likely to remain the market most vulnerable to uncertainty. The government securities market, where benchmark yields hardly changed on Monday, was expected to remain quiet. \par \par \uc2  Cuts in four of the NBH's five repo rates earlier on Monday had contributed to confidence that government securities remained unaffected by election uncertainty, analysts added. \par \par \uc2  The NBH said it had reduced both the overnight and one-week repo rates to 23.875 percent from 24.125 percent, the one-week reverse repo rate to 17.875 percent from 18.125 percent and the one-month reverse repo rate to 18.375 percent from 18.625 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The repo cut may be a step to prevent a rise in \par \par \uc2   yields...and it also follows a fall in year-on-year inflation to \par \par \uc2   16 percent in April from 16.4 percent in March," Ludanyi said. \par \par \uc2     ((Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4044, \par \par \uc2  budapest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5p04ljt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
