\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary may widen HUF band on cap inflow - Salomon. \b0\par\par\uc2 437 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 April 1998\par 22:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, April 29 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to widen the 4.5 percent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of its forint if the recent strong portfolio capital inflow continues, Salomon Smith Barney said in a report on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "In many respects, the Hungarian economy is displaying those characteristics that led the Polish authorities to repeatedly widen the exchange rate bands for the Polish zloty over the past few years," analyst Wike Groenenberg said in the report. \par \par \uc2  Salomon said it expected Hungary's gross domestic product (GDP) to grow by almost five percent this year against a backdrop of strong domestic demand and exports. \par \par \uc2  Hungary's solid economic fundamentals are encouraging a sharp increase in portfolio capital inflows, the analyst said. \par \par \uc2  She said the strong foreign interest was due to expectations that the Czech Republic, Poland and Hungary - all of them European Union member candidates - implement economic policies aimed at achieving convergence with the European Monetary Union's requirements. \par \par \uc2  The collapse of Italian, Spanish and Swedish bond yield spreads over Germany are prompting investors to look for a yield pick-up elsewhere and central Europe is the key beneficiary. \par \par \uc2  "However, following the substantial \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bond rallies in those (the Czech and the Polish) markets, attention has more recently focused on Hungary," she said. \par \par \uc2  Domestic demand growth and a keenness to cut inflation levels from 16.4 percent in March argue against Hungarian authorities allowing real interest rates to decline, she added. \par \par \uc2  Finance Ministry Peter Medgyessy said that, together with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Gyorgy Suranyi, he had proposed that the government decide on Thursday to cut the forint's monthly 0.9 percent devaluator to 0.8 percent. \par \par \uc2  But Medgyessy stressed in an interview to Reuters on Tuesday that he had agreed with Suranyi that they would not propose a widening of the forint's band. The 10 basis point cut in the devaluation rate would be a small change and investors would still be rewarded by more than LIBOR, Salomon said. \par \par \uc2  It added that, in the next few weeks, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to alter its monetary policy stance significantly in light of the two rounds of general elections on May 10 and 24. \par \par \uc2  But a continued strong portfolio capital inflow later may prompt a decision on widening the forint's trading band, although such a decision would not be easy as the small width of the band has served Hungary well by increasing exchange rate predictability, Salomon added. \par \par \uc2  ((Sandor Peto, Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4044 budapest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4t0677m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
