\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Steady Vs Basket Early, Seen Stable Next Week \b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 1997\par 11:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is steady against its fixing basket in early trading Friday and is seen remaining stable next week as investors keep their positions short due to the approaching book-closing at the end of the year. \par \par \uc2  Around 1000 GMT, the forint was trading about 2.0% from the midpoint on the strong side of the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, up slightly from around 1.97% in mid-session trading Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The band allows the forint to move a maximum of 2.25% from the midpoint, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  establishes using a fixing basket of 30% dollar and 70% Deutsche mark. \par \par \uc2  'We're at about the same point where we were yesterday,' said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at European Commercial Bank in Budapest. 'The forint's been moving in tandem with the dollar-mark levels.' \par \par \uc2  Because investors traditionally keep their positions short during December, it's unlikely the forint will move significantly next week on the band, the dealer added. \par \par \uc2  Around 1000 GMT, the dollar was at 199.55-199.60 forints, down from 199.76-199.81 forints in mid-session trading Thursday. The Deutsche mark was at 113.01-113.03 forints, essentially unchanged from 112.98-113.03 forints. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Thursday at 199.77 forints, up from 199.12 forints Wednesday. It fixed the mark at 113.06 forints Thursday, compared to 113.38 forints Wednesday. Friday's fixing will be released around 1100 GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Three-month interbank forint offered rates are indicated Friday at\par 19.99%, down from Thursday's 20.00%.\par -By Jack Grone; 361-267-0622; jgrone@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 28-11-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1025GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtbs0944g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
