\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Weakening Vs Basket In Lackluster Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 206 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 1997\par 12:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is weakening against its fixing basket in lackluster trading Tuesday, on the back of losses in Hong Kong stock prices. \par \par \uc2  At around 1107 GMT, the forint was trading 1.95% from the midpoint on the strong side of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band after a gradual weakening from 2.11% since the opening. \par \par \uc2  After the worldwide \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock exchange turmoil a week ago when the forint slipped to within 0.5% from the midpoint, the forint advanced Monday when it was traded steadily at around 2.10% from its midpoint. \par \par \uc2  'The strong performance of the New York Stock Exchange overnight had no influence on Japan and Hong Kong fell again, having a downward effect on the forint,' said dealer Peter Sipos at BNP-Dresdner Bank in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  The forint usually trades at its strongest point at 2.25% below the midpoint on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, which is 4.5% around the bank's parity level. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses a fixing basket made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark to establish parity. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 04-11-97 \par \par \uc2  1113GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtb408eki\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
