\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary economy seen sound despite forint, shares. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sandor Peto \par \uc2 406 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Oct 30 (Reuters) - Hungary's forint weakened relatively little due to the recent turbulence on world markets and economic fundamentals are still showing an improving picture, analysts said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "I do not see any fundamental reasons for a weakness of the forint," said Peter Muszely of Concorde Securities. \par \par \uc2  Hungary's forint closed at its weakest point for two and a half years on Tuesday at 1.25 percent above parity due to foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying triggered by a slump of share prices on the Budapest bourse on a global trend. \par \par \uc2  The forint firmed to two percent above parity on Wednesday, but renewed global uncertainty started by a new fall on the Hong Kong stock exchange pushed the forint down to 1.7 percent above parity on Thursday and traders said it might continue to ease. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the forint would ease further within the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (NBH) 4.5 percent wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band only if global share markets continued to decline. \par \par \uc2  "The Hungarian economy is improving and also the latest figures, August current account data, showed a positive picture," said Istvan Racz of Credit Suisse First Boston. \par \par \uc2  He added that problems on Far Eastern emerging markets, urging structural changes there, would not have a direct impact on Hungary. \par \par \uc2  "Economically, we are linked with Western Europe, and financially with Western Europe and the U.S. (and not the Far East)," Racz said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the developing stock exchange as a financing resource still had a relatively small importance for Hungarian companies and international events would affect the Hungarian bond market little as foreigners were minor players there. \par \par \uc2  They added a large-scale NBH \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect the forint was unlikely even if international events weaken the Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  further. \par \par \uc2  But if the forint eases to levels around parity on any particular day, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may decide to demonstrate the seriousness of its anti-inflation stance and may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Racz said. \par \par \uc2  "A substantial intra-day devaluation could mean certain inflationary pressure on a psychological basis," he said, adding, however, that the current weakness of the forint was even positive for the NBH. \par \par \uc2  "It is not good for a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  if its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is always at the resistance level, putting it under a continuous pressure to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  -- Budapest newswroom (36 1) 327 4044 \par \par \uc2  budapest.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtau03ag5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
