\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Recovers From Early Lows But Set to Stay Weak \b0\par\par\uc2 255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 1997\par 13:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint staged a partial recovery midday Tuesday from earlier lows against its fixing basket, although traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to remain weaker than normal for the next three days. \par \par \uc2  'The drop on the Budapest Stock Exchange will have its effect on the forint in the next three days because investors will still be selling forints,' said dealer Laszlo Egyed At WestLB Hungary in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  The bourse's benchmark BUX index dropped Tuesday about 16.5% from its close Monday. \par \par \uc2  Shortly after 1200 GMT, the forint was trading around 1.25% from its midpoint on the strong side of the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from the midpoint. \par \par \uc2  Earlier the forint dropped to within 0.5% of the midpoint, but always remained on the strong side of the band, Egyed said. \par \par \uc2  Usually the forint trades within a few basis points of its strongest point on the band. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses a fixing basket made up of 30% dollar and 70% Deutsche mark to establish its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  range. \par \par \uc2  At around 1225 GMT, the dollar was at 195.42-195.47 forints, down from 196.34-196.39 forints around 1000 GMT. The mark was at 113.09 to 113.14 forints, down slightly from 113.25-113.30 forints earlier Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 28-10-97 \par \par \uc2  1244GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par