\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Weaker Against Dlr, Slightly Up Vs Mark \b0\par\par\uc2 239 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Oktober 1997\par 11:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is weakening against the dollar and strengthening against the Deutsche mark in languid trading Friday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the forint's moves are being driven by the dollar's trading ranges against the mark, and that turnover is weak Friday. \par \par \uc2  At around 0945 GMT, the dollar was at 195.74-195.79 forints, up from 194.83-194.88 forints in late trading Thursday. The mark was at 111.28-111.33 forints, down from 111.46-111.51 forints. \par \par \uc2  'Demand seems to be evenly balanced between the forint and the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' said a trader at a major domestic bank in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  The forint is trading near its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses a fixing basket made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark to establish the band. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Thursday at 194.78 forints, down from 194.98 forints Wednesday. It fixed the mark at 111.53 forints Thursday, compared with 111.30 forints Wednesday. Friday's fixing will be released around 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 20.02% Friday, compared with 20.05% at the previous session. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-10-97 \par \par \uc2  0956GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtah07wfk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict