\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Up Vs Dlr, Weaker Vs DM In Late Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 234 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Oktober 1997\par 14:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is strengthening against the dollar and weakening against the Deutsche mark late Thursday, in a quiet market. \par \par \uc2  The Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been moving in line with the general trend of the dollar and the Deutsche mark. \par \par \uc2  At around 1215 GMT, the dollar was at 194.83-194.88 forints, down from 195.09-195.14 forints in midsession trading Wednesday. The mark was at 111.46 to 111.51 forints, up from 111.21 to 111.26 forints. \par \par \uc2  The forint is trading at its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fixing against a basket made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. \par \par \uc2  'There's no interest whatsoever. It's just like summer,' said Peter Sipos, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at BNP-Dredsner Bank in Budapest, adding that international dollar-mark trading has been very quiet Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Thursday at 194.78 forints, down from 194.98 forints Wednesday. It fixed the mark at 111.53 forints Thursday, compared with 111.30 forints Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The three-month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 20.05% Thursday, unchanged from Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 16-10-97 \par \par \uc2  1239GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtag07qum\par }\page {\par\fs20