\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Weaker Vs Dlr, Stronger Vs DM At Midday \b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 1997\par 12:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is weaker against the dollar and stronger against the Deutsche mark in quiet trading at midday Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  At around 1015 GMT, the dollar was at 195.09 to 195.14 forints, up from 194.58 to 194.63 forints at mid-session Tuesday. The mark was at 111.21-111.26 forints, down from 111.30-111.35 forints. \par \par \uc2  The forint is trading at its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses a fixing basket made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark to establish the band. \par \par \uc2  'There's a medium level of turnover on the market,' said Zoltan Kalman, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Hypo Bank Hungary Rt. in Budapest. 'The dollar-mark trading has been relatively calm, and the forint has stayed completely at (the strongest point) of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band.' \par \par \uc2  Kalman said he expects the market in Budapest to remain placid during trading this afternoon. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Wednesday at 194.98 forints, up from 194.54 forints Tuesday. It fixed the mark at 111.30 forints Wednesday, compared with 111.34 forints Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 20.05% Wednesday, unchanged from Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-10-97 \par \par \uc2  1027GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji