\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Stronger Vs Dollar In Thin Early Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 249 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 1997\par 12:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is stronger against the dollar and weaker against the Deutsche mark in quiet trading Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  At 1000 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 194.58 to 194.63 forints, down from 195.14 to 195.19 forints in mid-session trading Monday. They quoted the mark at 111.30 to 111.35 forints, up from 111.11 to 111.16 forints. \par \par \uc2  The forint is trading at its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses a fixing basket made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark to establish the band. \par \par \uc2  Trading Tuesday morning has been quiet, with the forint following as usual the moves of the dollar-mark rates on international markets, said Balazs Benczedi, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at WestLB Hungaria in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  Benczedi said he expects activity to pick up in the afternoon as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders in New York return to their desks following Monday's Columbus Day holiday in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Tuesday at 194.54 forints, down from 195.32 forints Monday. It fixed the mark at 111.34 forints Tuesday, compared with 111.10 forints Monday. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 20.05% Tuesday, unchanged from Monday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-10-97 \par \par \uc2  1008GMT \par \par \uc2