\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Recovers Late In Morning From Early Weakness \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 1997\par 11:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--Following a slight weakening against its fixing basket early Friday, the Hungarian forint has recovered and is trading at the strong end of its fluctuation range in late-morning trade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Shortly after 930 GMT the forint was trading at its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses a fixing basket made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark to establish the band. \par \par \uc2  'It's been pretty active Friday,' said Laszlo Egyed, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at WestLB Hungaria Rt. in Budapest. 'At one point the forint was about 10 to 15 basis points from the strong point on the band, but now it's gone back.' \par \par \uc2  Egyed attributed the temporary weakening to the usual demand for hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  near the end of each month by Hungarian companies that need to pay import bills. \par \par \uc2  At 942 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 194.05 to 194.10 forints, down from 195.60 to 195.65 forints in midsession trading Thursday. They quoted the mark at 110.60 to 110.62 forints, up from 110.16 to 110.21 forints. \par \par \uc2  Those moves reflect the dollar's weakening against the mark on other European markets early Friday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Thursday at 195.56 forints, down from 196.07 forints Wednesday. It fixed the mark at 110.19 forints Thursday, compared with 109.92 forints Wednesday. Friday's fixing will be released after 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three-month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 20.12% Friday, unchanged from Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 26-09-97 \par \par \uc2  0955GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt9q075r0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
