\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Dn Vs Dlr, Traders Eye Dollar-Mark Moves \b0\par\par\uc2 253 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 1997\par 12:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is weakening against the dollar in moderately active trading Tuesday, and market participants expect dollar-Deutsche mark moves to lead the market. \par \par \uc2  At 0951 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 196.84 to 196.89 forints, up from 196.48 to 196.53 forints in mid-session trading Monday. They quoted the mark at 109.61 to 109.66 forints, down from 109.72 to 109.77 forints. \par \par \uc2  The forint has spent Tuesday's session so far glued to its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses a fixing basket made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark to establish the band. \par \par \uc2  'There's been a moderate level of activity Tuesday, but it's all been generated by the dollar-mark trading,' said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a Hungarian bank in Budapest. Traders expects the forint to continue following the dollar-mark moves throughout the afternoon. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Monday at 196.14 forints, up from 195.64 forints Friday. It fixed the mark at 109.80 forints Monday, compared with 109.85 forints Friday. Tuesday's fixing will be released shortly. \par \par \uc2  The three-month interbank forint offered rates have fallen Tuesday to 20.13% from Monday's 20.14%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 23-09-97 \par \par \uc2  1004GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt9n076v